![license](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-Apache_2.0-blue) ![offline-first](https://img.shields.io/badge/offline-first-air-gap-green) ![audit](https://img.shields.io/badge/audit-SHA3-256-orange) ![integration](https://img.shields.io/badge/integration-offline-packaged-lightgrey)

> Cloud-native search engine

**Upstream:** https://github.com/quickwit-oss/quickwit

**Upstream pin:** commit NOT YET MEASURED (no verifiable UPSTREAM/.anticloud-provenance.json or UPSTREAM_CLONE commit on disk; never guessed) (Apache 2.0) · **Category:** SEARCH_ENGINES · **Vendor:** Anticloud FZ LLE

## Architecture

```mermaid
graph LR
    U[Upstream: QUICKWIT] --> S[Anticloud shim]
    S --> T[Deterministic tool<br/>no model decoding path]
    T --> A[AIOSS ledger<br/>SHA3-256 chained]
    A --> B[Single binary]
```

**Scope honesty:** QUICKWIT ships as an offline package with AIOSS audit wiring. It has no model decoding path — PAX L5 Narrow L2 General 27B may call it as a deterministic tool, nothing more.

